### 5. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

#### 5.1 Physical module layout

The EOPL seat module consists of five integrated layers from bottom to top:

Layer 0 — Foundation Rail
A pair of precision linear guide rails (Thomson or equivalent) with low-friction carriages, supporting the entire moving seat assembly. Travel range: 80 mm. Maximum rated load: 5 kN radial. Material: hardened steel rail, polymer-coated carriage.

Layer 1 — Lower Halbach Array (Fixed, mounted to vehicle floor frame)
Six Halbach sub-arrays, each of 4 pole pairs (N52 NdFeB, B_r = 1.48 T), arranged in a 2 × 3 grid spanning 300 mm × 250 mm. Array thickness h_m = 20 mm. Back iron: 5 mm low-carbon steel. Total array mass: ~3.2 kg. Peak surface field B₀ ≈ 1.36 T.

Layer 2 — Conductive Damping Plate (Moving with seat)
Oxygen-free high-conductivity copper (OFHC), σ = 5.8 × 10⁷ S/m. Dimensions: 300 mm × 250 mm × 4 mm. Mass: 0.85 kg. Mounted rigidly to the moving seat sub-frame. Air gap to each Halbach array face: g = 2.5 mm nominal (maintained by the linear guide). Plate is electrically isolated from the seat structure to prevent parasitic current paths.

Layer 3 — Upper Halbach Array (Fixed to lower seat pan, moving with occupant load but fixed relative to the plate in normal operation; fixed to vehicle in crash mode via a locking mechanism)
Mirror of Layer 1. In normal driving, both arrays move with the seat together (no relative motion, no damping). Upon crash activation, a fast-release lock (electromagnetic or pyrotechnic pin) decouples the upper assembly from the seat pan, fixing both arrays to the vehicle frame, so the plate (still attached to the moving seat) travels through the field.

This lock-and-release architecture is critical: in normal operation the system adds zero drag, activating only when the pre-crash module fires. This avoids NVH (noise, vibration, harshness) degradation in normal driving.

Layer 4 — Adaptive Electromagnet Coil Bank (Overlaid on Halbach arrays)
Eight pancake coils (24 AWG copper, N_turns = 150 each) mounted on the back-iron face of both arrays. These allow augmentation of the static Halbach field by up to ΔB = ±0.4 T, enabling adaptive damping coefficient adjustment:

C_em(t) = σ · d · w · l · [B₀ + ΔB(t)]²

where ΔB(t) = μ₀ · N_turns · I_coil(t) / (2 · g + h_m) is the coil field contribution. This gives real-time control authority over C_em through variation of I_coil. Maximum continuous coil power: ~200 W per coil bank. Energy source: onboard ultracapacitor bank (see Section 7).

Layer 5 — Seat Structure and Occupant Interface
Standard automotive seat foam, frame, and harness attachment points, mounted atop Layer 3. Mass budget: ≤ 5 kg added total system mass over baseline seat.

