### 11. MATHEMATICAL COMPLETENESS NOTES

The full model requires FEA validation (ANSYS Maxwell or COMSOL Multiphysics) to verify:

(a) Actual B₀ field distribution including fringe effects at array edges (can deviate ≥ 15% from analytical model for short arrays)

(b) Eddy current distribution in the finite copper plate including corner effects

(c) Thermal distribution during repeated low-severity impact testing

(d) Guide rail deflection under 5 kN lateral loads

The analytical model above provides a closed-form design starting point. The FEA would refine C_em by an estimated ±20% from the analytical prediction, which is consistent with reported 7.5% RMS error in the damping coefficient estimation for validated magnetic spring-damper analytical models. Such analytical models based on electromagnetic theory exhibit approximately 7.5% RMS error for the damping coefficient estimation when experimentally verified. [Illinois](http://jontalle.web.engr.illinois.edu/Public/Allen/Noori-pdf/EddyCurrentDampiing.08.pdf)

